From 3dad68539827a0e3479b58cc6afb4c6dce904b08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:46:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/timer: TCC capture and circular buffers (U2213)

Capture as a PIC32CM MC00 does it (firmware/hello APP=tccprobe10 and
tccprobe11, checked by tcccapt). A CPTENx channel captures COUNT on the
rising edge of its MCx event (EVCTRL.MCEIx), and EV1's PPW and PWP
actions capture the period (restarting the counter, TRG) and the pulse
width into CC0 and CC1, on the edges TCINV1 selects. Each capture
channel is a FIFO: CCx with INTFLAG.MCx, then CCBUFx with
STATUS.CCBUFVx, then INTFLAG.ERR; reading CCx clears MCx and moves
CCBUFx up two GCLK_TCC cycles later. In dual slope with TOP below MAX/2
the capture's MSB marks the down ramp. Fault capture uses the same
FIFO, and capture channels no longer set compare-match flags.

Circular buffers (WAVE.CIPEREN, CICCENx; tccprobe12): each update swaps
the register and its buffer, every cycle in single slope, at TOP and
ZERO for CCx and at ZERO for PER in DSBOTH; the valid flag clears at the
first update, in RAMP2 and DSBOTH at the first that starts cycle A. PER
and CCx reads show the buffer while it is valid or circular, and PER or
CCx writes reach their buffers too, as on silicon.

The enable no longer copies the buffers: silicon waits for the first
update condition. STATUS.FAULTnIN shows an enabled EVn input whatever
its action.

qtest: capture FIFO and the dual-slope MSB, PPW/PWP, buffers at the
enable, circular buffers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
